From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FX Steam Launcher <dev@fxgam.es>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MSL: Preserve explicit interface block member locations

The running location used while flattening an interface block was established
by its first member and then advanced across every following member. Later
explicit Location decorations were ignored, so Location 0 followed by Location
2 became user(locn0) and user(locn1). Matching standalone declarations retained
their locations and could no longer link to the block in Metal.

Start a new range at each explicitly located top-level block member before
flattening it. The member's own array elements, matrix columns, and nested
structure contents still advance the location normally. Component decorations
remain attached to the original location, including two members sharing one
location with disjoint components.

Regression: host/moltenvk/repro/sentry-block-locations.sh compares generated
MSL attributes with spirv-dis Location/Component decorations and links all four
block/standalone vertex/fragment combinations through Metal. Covers location
gaps, arrays, matrices, component sharing, and reordered member locations.
Candidate for STEAMAC-88/2M; the exact event SPIR-V is unavailable. This does
not establish the cause of STEAMAC-87's repeated identical user names.

---
diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
index 9983ccf..bd682a0 100644
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -5584,6 +5584,12 @@ void CompilerMSL::add_variable_to_interface_block(StorageClass storage, const st
 					}
 					else if (!is_builtin || has_active_builtin(builtin, storage))
 					{
+						// An explicit member location starts a new range, even after an earlier
+						// member established the running location. Only the flattened elements
+						// within this member (arrays, matrices, or structs) are consecutive.
+						if (has_member_decoration(var_type.self, mbr_idx, DecorationLocation))
+							location = get_member_decoration(var_type.self, mbr_idx, DecorationLocation);
+
 						bool is_composite_type = is_matrix(mbr_type) || is_array(mbr_type) || mbr_type.basetype == SPIRType::Struct;
 						bool attribute_load_store =
 								storage == StorageClassInput && get_execution_model() != ExecutionModelFragment;
